- High wind risk on most days (53-56%) which would cause pesticide drift and wash off your treatment

**What this means:**
Even if peanuts are a good time to treat for peanut diseases, you cannot spray during these rainy/windy conditions. The rain will wash away the fungicide before it works effectively, and strong winds could spread disease through drift rather than targeted application.

